From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Subject: [PATCH] verify measured M4 postboot runtime APEX in release gate

# Reason: the diagnostic profile intentionally replaces only the BZI6 tethering APEX with the measured compatibility output; the generic M4 verifier still demanded the donor hash. This rejected the exact, locked diagnostic output after its own postboot verifier had passed.
# Affected: compiled release-default verification for the explicit M4/G965F diagnostic profile.
# Verify: donor-native runtime check remains strict for all other profiles; for M4 diagnostic, allow only the APEX exception after exact runtime-compat validation and require the postboot helper to verify both locked outputs. Run the compiled release gate and final ext4 image gate.
# Rollback: reverse this gate exception; the diagnostic profile then cannot package the measured APEX.

--- a/rom/scripts/internal/verify_exynos9810_release_defaults.py
+++ b/rom/scripts/internal/verify_exynos9810_release_defaults.py
@@ -3,6 +3,7 @@
 from pathlib import Path
 from hashlib import sha256
 import argparse,json,os,sys,zipfile
+import importlib.util
 ROOT=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[2]
 sys.path.insert(0,str(ROOT/"scripts/internal/FaceunlockFix"))
 from release_bridge import load_release_bridge
@@ -53,7 +54,22 @@
